Naegleria fowleri ("brain-eating amoeba") deaths by U.S. state

- This notebook generates a U.S. choropleth map of locations where people have died from Naegleria fowleri (PAM).
- Data source priority: CDC pages (cases by state of exposure) → peer-reviewed summaries → Wikipedia as a last resort.
- Note: PAM is >97% fatal; when a source lists only total cases by state, this notebook treats cases as a close proxy for deaths. A small number of survivors exist; if a deaths column is present, it will be used instead.

How to use
- Run the cell below. It will attempt to fetch an authoritative table. If all fetches fail, it will render a map from a small embedded sample and clearly warn you to update the data.

Attribution
- CDC general info: `https://www.cdc.gov/parasites/naegleria/`
- Peer‑reviewed overview (for geographic range context): `https://doi.org/10.3201/eid2701.202119`